e effective annual rate:\n\\[\n\\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + 0.005\\right)^{12} - 1\n\\]\n\nUsing a step-by-step computation:\n\\[\n1.005^{12} \\approx 1.061678\n\\]\nSubtracting 1 from this value gives:\n\\[\n\\text{EAR} \\approx 1.061678 - 1 = 0.061678\n\\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[\n\\text{EAR} \\approx 6.17\\%\n\\]\n\nThus, the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) is \\(\\boxed{6.17}\\).",
