Well, since I computed the step-by-step multiplication and got 6.1052%, I think that's more accurate. Maybe the natural log method is introducing some error because of the approximation in ln(1.005). Alternatively, perhaps I made a miscalculation in the exponent.\n\nWait, no, the step-by-step multiplication is the exact way, so 6.1052% is more accurate. So, about 6.11% when rounded to the nearest hundredth.\n\nWait, but 6.1052 is approximately 6.11. So, is 6.11% the answer?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I should use more precise calculation methods.\n\nWait, another way to compute 1.005^12 is using the formula for compound interest: A = P(1 + r/n)^(nt). So, here, A = P(1 + 0.06/12)^12. So, A = P*(1.005)^12. So, the effective rate is (1.005)^12 - 1, which is approximately 0.06105, as we saw.\n\nSo, 6.105%, which rounds to 6.11%.\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual rate is approximately 6.11%.\n\nWait, but the question says \"to the nearest hundredth\", so that would be 6.11%.\n\nBut just to be thorough, let me check if my step-by-step multiplication was correct. Let me write out each step:\n\n1: 1.005\n\n2: 1.005 * 1.005 = 1.010025\n\n3: 1.010025 * 1.005 = let's compute 1.010025 * 1.005.\n\n1 * 1.005 = 1.005\n\n0.010025 * 1.005 = 0.010075125\n\nSo, total is 1.005 + 0.010075125 = 1.015075125\n\n4: 1.015075125 * 1.005\n\n1 * 1.005 = 1.005\n\n0.015075125 * 1.005 ≈ 0.015150625\n\nTotal ≈ 1.005 + 0.015150625 = 1.020150625\n\n5: 1.020150625 * 1.005\n\n1 * 1.005 = 1.005\n\n0.020150625 * 1.005 ≈ 0.020251531\n\nTotal ≈ 1.005 + 0.020251531 ≈ 1.025251531\n\n6: 1.025251531 * 1.005\n\n1 * 1.005 = 1.005\n\n0.025251531 * 1.005 ≈ 0.025377132\n\nTotal ≈ 1.005 + 0.025377132 ≈ 1.030377132\n\n7: 1.030377132 * 1.005\n\n1 * 1.005 = 1.005\n\n0.030377132 * 1.005 ≈ 0.030546443\n\nTotal ≈ 1.005 + 0.030546443 ≈ 1.035546443\n\n8: 1.035546443 * 1.005\n\n1 * 1.005 = 1.005\n\n0.035546443 * 1.005 ≈ 0.035641895\n\nTotal ≈ 1.005 + 0.035641895 ≈ 1.040641895\n\n9: 1.040641895 * 1.005\n\n1 * 1.005 = 1.005\n\n0.040641895 * 1.005 ≈ 0.040747448\n\nTotal ≈ 1.005 + 0.040747448 ≈ 1.045747448\n\n10: 1.045747448 * 1.005\n\n1 * 1.005 = 1.005\n\n0.045747448 * 1.005 ≈ 0.045928302\n\nTotal ≈ 1.005 + 0.045928302 ≈ 1.050928302\n\n11: 1.050928302 * 1.005\n\n1 * 1.005 = 1.005\n\n0.050928302 * 1.005 ≈ 0.051055728\n\nTotal ≈ 1.005 + 0.051055728 ≈ 1.056055728\n\nWait, wait, hold on, earlier I had 1.055728 for the 11th step, but now it's 1.056055728. Hmm, seems like an inconsistency.\n\nWait, no, in the step-by-step before, I think I had 1.055728 for step 11, but now with more precise calculation, it's 1.056055728. So, perhaps my earlier step was an approximation.\n\nContinuing:\n\n12: 1.056055728 * 1.005\n\n1 * 1.005 = 1.005\n\n0.056055728 * 1.005 ≈ 0.056056443\n\nTotal ≈ 1.005 + 0.056056443 ≈ 1.061056443\n\nSo, 1.061056443, so the effective annual rate is 0.061056443, which is approximately 6.1065%, so 6.11% when rounded to the nearest hundredth.\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual rate r is approximately 6.11%.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the answer is 6.11%.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.11}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return as a 6% annual interest rate compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\n1. The nominal annual interest rate is 6%, or 0.06 in decimal.\n2. Since the interest is compounded monthly, we have 12 compounding periods per year.\n3. The effective annual rate is calculated using the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} - 1\n   \\]\n4. First, compute \\(\\frac{0.06}{12}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{0.06}{12} = 0.005\n   \\]\n5. Then, compute \\(\\left(1 + 0.005\\right)^{12}\\):\n   \\[\n   (1.005)^{12}\n   \\]\n6. Calculating step-by-step:\n   \\[\n   1.005^2 = 1.010025\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1.010025^2 = 1.020150\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1.020150^2 = 1.040604\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1.040604^2 = 1.082402\n   \\]\n   However, a more precise calculation using step-by-step multiplication shows:\n   \\[\n   1.005^{12} \\approx 1.061051\n   \\]\n7. Subtract 1 to get the effective annual rate:\n   \\[\n   1.061051 - 1 = 0.061051\n   \\]\n8. Converting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n   \\[\n   0.061051 \\approx 6.11\\%\n   \\]\n\nThus, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\(\\boxed{6.11}\\).",
