proximately 6.17%. So, there's a slight difference between the two methods. Which one is more accurate? Probably the direct calculation, because the EAR formula is exact for compound interest. The approximation with e^{r} is more of an approximation, especially for lower n.\n\nTherefore, sticking with the exact calculation, we get 6.16778%, which rounds to 6.17%.\n\nHence, the equivalent annual interest rate r is approximately 6.17%.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.17}.\n\\\n\nProblem: Dr. Fu Manchu has a bank account that has an annual interest rate of 6 percent, but it compounds monthly. If this is equivalent to a bank account that compounds annually at a rate of \\( r \\) percent, then what is \\( r \\)? (Give your answer to the nearest hundredth.)\n\nReasoning step by step:\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return when compounded annually as the given rate compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\n1. The nominal annual interest rate is 6%, which is 0.06 in decimal.\n2. Since the interest is compounded monthly, the number of compounding periods per year \\( n \\) is 12.\n3. The effective annual rate is calculated using the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n - 1\n   \\]\n   Here, \\( r = 0.06 \\) and \\( n = 12 \\).\n\n4. Plugging in the values:\n   \\[\n   \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} - 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + 0.005\\right)^{12} - 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{EAR} = 1.005^{12} - 1\n   \\]\n\n5. Calculating \\( 1.005^{12} \\):\n   - Using step-by-step multiplication or a calculator, we find:\n     \\[\n     1.005^{12} \\approx 1.0616785\n     \\]\n   - Subtracting 1 from this value gives the EAR:\n     \\[\n     \\text{EAR} \\approx 1.0616785 - 1 = 0.0616785\n     \\]\n   - Converting this back to a percentage:\n     \\[\n     0.0616785 \\times 100 \\approx 6.16785\\%\n     \\]\n\n6. Rounding 6.16785% to the nearest hundredth gives 6.17%.\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.17}.",
