05 = 1.005 \\]\n\n3. Raise 1.005 to the power of 12:\n   \\[ 1.005^{12} \\approx 1.061678 \\]\n\n4. Subtract 1 from the result to get the EAR:\n   \\[ 1.061678 - 1 = 0.061678 \\]\n\n5. Convert the result to a percentage and round to the nearest hundredth:\n   \\[ 0.061678 \\times 100 \\approx 6.17\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\(\\boxed{6.17}\\).",
