\nFirst, compute 1.040705 * 1 = 1.040705.\n\nThen, 1.040705 * 0.02 = 0.0208171.\n\nThen, 1.040705 * 0.0001505 ≈ approx 0.000157.\n\nAdding up: 1.040705 + 0.0208171 + 0.000157 ≈ 1.061679.\n\nSo, more accurately, 1.040705 * 1.0201505 ≈ 1.061679.\n\nSo, 1.005^12 ≈ 1.061679, which is about 6.1679%.\n\nWait, so now I get two different results. When I compute step-by-step, I got 1.064588868, which is about 6.4588%.\n\nBut when I compute (1.005^4)*(1.005^8) ≈ 1.0201505 * 1.040810127 ≈ 1.061679.\n\nWhich is correct?\n\nWait, perhaps my step-by-step is wrong.\n\nWait, 1.005^12 is equal to (1.005^12). Let me compute 1.005^12 using exponentiation step by step.\n\nCompute 1.005^2 = 1.010025.\n\n1.005^4 = (1.010025)^2 = 1.020150500625.\n\n1.005^8 = (1.020150500625)^2.\n\nCompute 1.020150500625 * 1.020150500625:\n\nFirst, 1*1 = 1.\n\n1 * 0.020150500625 = 0.020150500625.\n\n0.020150500625 * 1 = 0.020150500625.\n\n0.020150500625 * 0.020150500625 ≈ 0.000404.\n\nAdding up: 1 + 0.020150500625 + 0.020150500625 + 0.000404 ≈ 1.040705.\n\nWait, so 1.005^8 is approximately 1.040705.\n\nThen, 1.005^12 is 1.005^8 * 1.005^4 ≈ 1.040705 * 1.020150500625.\n\nCompute that:\n\n1.040705 * 1.020150500625.\n\n1 * 1.040705 = 1.040705.\n\n0.020150500625 * 1.040705.\n\nCompute 1.040705 * 0.02 = 0.0208171.\n\nCompute 1.040705 * 0.000150500625 ≈ approximately 0.000157.\n\nSo, total is 0.0208171 + 0.000157 ≈ 0.0209741.\n\nAdding to 1.040705: 1.040705 + 0.0209741 ≈ 1.061679.\n\nSo, 1.005^12 ≈ 1.061679.\n\nBut when I computed step by step, I got 1.005^12 ≈ 1.064588868.\n\nWait, this discrepancy is confusing. Let me see which one is correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can use logarithms or another method.\n\nTake natural logarithm on both sides: ln(1.005^12) = 12 * ln(1.005).\n\nCompute ln(1.005). Using Taylor series, ln(1+x) ≈ x - x^2/2 + x^3/3 - x^4/4 + ..., for small x.\n\nHere, x=0.005, so ln(1.005) ≈ 0.005 - (0.005)^2 / 2 + (0.005)^3 / 3 - (0.005)^4 / 4.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n0.005 = 0.005\n\n(0.005)