\n\nSo, 6.1677304% is approximately 6.17%.\n\nWait, but some calculators may compute it as 6.17 or 6.18.\n\nWait, to be precise, let me compute 1.005^12 using a calculator.\n\nUsing a calculator:\n\n1.005^12.\n\nCompute step by step:\n\n1.005^2 = 1.010025\n\n1.005^3 = 1.010025 * 1.005 ≈ 1.015075125\n\n1.005^4 ≈ 1.015075125 * 1.005 ≈ 1.020150501\n\n1.005^5 ≈ 1.020150501 * 1.005 ≈ 1.025316408\n\n1.005^6 ≈ 1.025316408 * 1.005 ≈ 1.030377578\n\n1.005^7 ≈ 1.030377578 * 1.005 ≈ 1.035528326\n\n1.005^8 ≈ 1.035528326 * 1.005 ≈ 1.040810127\n\n1.005^9 ≈ 1.040810127 * 1.005 ≈ 1.046488109\n\n1.005^10 ≈ 1.046488109 * 1.005 ≈ 1.052392583\n\n1.005^11 ≈ 1.052392583 * 1.005 ≈ 1.058455935\n\n1.005^12 ≈ 1.058455935 * 1.005 ≈ 1.064588868\n\nWait, now I get 1.064588868, which is approximately 1.064589, so subtracting 1, we have 0.064589, which is 6.4589%.\n\nWait, so that's a different result. So, now I'm confused.\n\nWait, wait, hold on, when I compute 1.005^12 step by step, I get 1.064588868, but when I compute (1.005^4)*(1.005^8), I get 1.061679.\n\nSo, why the discrepancy?\n\nWait, because in my step-by-step, when I compute 1.005^12, I get 1.064588868, but when I compute (1.005^4)*(1.005^8) = 1.020150501 * 1.040810127 ≈ 1.061679.\n\nSo, which one is correct?\n\nWait, perhaps I made an error in the step-by-step computation.\n\nWait, let me verify 1.005^12.\n\nCompute 1.005^2 = 1.010025.\n\n1.005^3: 1.010025 * 1.005.\n\nCompute 1.010025 * 1.005:\n\n1 * 1.010025 = 1.010025\n\n0.005 * 1.010025 = 0.005050125\n\nAdding together: 1.010025 + 0.005050125 = 1.015075125.\n\nCorrect.\n\n1.005^4: 1.015075125 * 1.005.\n\nCompute 1.015075125 * 1.005:\n\n1 * 1.015075125 = 1.015075125\n\n0.005 * 1.015075125 = 0.005075375625\n\nAdding: 1.015075125 + 0.005075375625 ≈ 1.020150500625.\n\n1.005^5: 1.020150500625 * 1.005.\n\nCompute:\n\n1 * 1.020150500625 = 1.020150500625\n\n0.005 * 1.020150500625 ≈ 0.00510075250625\n\nAdding: 1.020150500625 + 0.00510075250625 ≈ 1.025251253131.\n\n1.005^6: 1.025251253131 * 1.005.\n\nCompute:\n\n1 * 1.025251253131 = 1.025251253131\n\n0.005 * 1.025251253131 ≈ 0.005126256265655\n\nAdding: 1.025251253131 + 0.005126256265655 ≈ 1.030377509396.\n\n1.005^7: 1.030377509396 * 1.005.\n\nCompute:\n\n1 * 1.030377509396 = 1.030377509396\n\n0.005 * 1.030377509396 ≈ 0.00515188754798\n\nAdding: 1.030377509396 + 0.00515188754798 ≈ 1.035529397.\n\n1.005^8: 1.035529397 * 1.005.\n\nCompute:\n\n1 * 1.035529397 = 1.035529397\n\n0.005 * 1.035529397 ≈ 0.005177647\n\nAdding: 1.035529397 + 0.005177647 ≈ 1.040707044.\n\n1.005^9: 1.040707044 * 1.005.\n\nCompute:\n\n1 * 1.040707044 = 1.040707044\n\n0.005 * 1.040707044 ≈ 0.00520353522\n\nAdding: 1.040707044 + 0.00520353522 ≈ 1.04591057922.\n\n1.005^10: 1.04591057922 * 1.005.\n\nCompute:\n\n1 * 1.04591057922 = 1.04591057922\n\n0.005 * 1.04591057922 ≈ 0.0052290528961\n\nAdding: 1.04591057922 + 0.0052290528961 ≈ 1.051139632116.\n\n1.005^11: 1.051139632116 * 1.005.\n\nCompute:\n\n1 * 1.051139632116 = 1.051139632116\n\n0.005 * 1.051139632116 ≈ 0.00525569816\n\nAdding: 1.051139632116 + 0.00525569816 ≈ 1.056395330276.\n\n1.005^12: 1.056395330276 * 1.005.\n\nCompute:\n\n1 * 1.056395330276 = 1.056395330276\n\n0.005 * 1.056395330276 ≈ 0.00528197640\n\nAdding: 1.056395330276 + 0.00528197640 ≈ 1.061677306676.\n\nSo, 1.005^12 ≈ 1.061677306676, which is approximately 1.0616773.\n\nTherefore, 1.0616773 - 1 = 0.0616773, which is 6.16773%.\n\nSo, 6.16773%, which is approximately 6.17% when rounded to the nearest hundredth.\n\nBut in another calculation, earlier, when I thought I was computing 1.005^12 as 1.064588868, that was incorrect because I must have miscalculated. Wait, no, that step-by-step is correct. Wait, no, when I computed 1.005^12 step-by-step earlier, I ended up with 1.064588868, which contradicts the previous calculation.\n\nWait, perhaps I confused another exponent. Wait, no, let me check:\n\nWait, in the step-by-step above, I correctly compute 1.005^12 as 1.0616773.\n\nBut in the earlier mistaken step-by-step, I thought that 1.005^12 is 1.064588868. So, that must have been a miscalculation. So, the accurate step-by-step gives 1.0616773, which is 6.16773%.\n\nTherefore, the correct EAR is approximately 6.17%.\n\nTherefore, r ≈ 6.17%.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 6.17 percent.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.17}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return if Dr. Fu Manchu's bank account were compounded annually instead of monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe bank account has an annual nominal interest rate of 6 percent, compounded monthly. The formula for compound interest is:\n\n\\[ A = P \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( A \\) is the amount of money accumulated after \\( n \\) years, including interest.\n- \\( P \\) is the principal amount.\n- \\( r \\) is the annual interest rate (decimal).\n- \\( n \\) is the number of times that interest is compounded per year.\n\nSince we are looking for the equivalent annual rate, we set the amount after one year with monthly compounding equal to the amount after one year with annual compounding. This gives us:\n\n\\[ P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = P \\left(1 + r \\right) \\]\n\nThe principal \\( P \\) cancels out, leaving:\n\n\\[ \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nCalculating the left-hand side:\n\n\\[ \\frac{0.06}{12} = 0.005 \\]\n\\[ (1 + 0.005)^{12} \\approx 1.061677 \\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[ 1 + r \\approx 1.061677 \\]\n\\[",
