ual rate:\n\nEAR = (1 + r/n)^n - 1\n\nWhere r is the nominal annual rate and n is the number of compounding periods per year.\n\nSo, plugging in r = 0.06, n=12:\n\nEAR = (1 + 0.06/12)^12 - 1 = (1.005)^12 - 1\n\nWhich is approximately 1.061516 - 1 = 0.061516, or 6.1516%.\n\nSo, that's 6.15% when rounded to the nearest hundredth.\n\nWait, but I recall that sometimes calculators give more precise numbers. Let me see if I can compute 1.005^12 more precisely.\n\nLet me compute 1.005^12 step by step with more decimal places.\n\nCompute 1.005^1 = 1.005\n\n1.005^2 = 1.005 * 1.005 = 1.010025\n\n1.005^3 = 1.010025 * 1.005. Let's compute 1.010025 * 1.005:\n\nMultiply 1.010025 by 1.005:\n\n1.010025 * 1 = 1.010025\n\n1.010025 * 0.005 = 0.005050125\n\nAdding them: 1.010025 + 0.005050125 = 1.015075125\n\n1.005^4 = 1.015075125 * 1.005\n\nCompute 1.015075125 * 1.005:\n\n1.015075125 * 1 = 1.015075125\n\n1.015075125 * 0.005 = 0.005075375625\n\nAdding: 1.015075125 + 0.005075375625 ≈ 1.020150500625\n\n1.005^5 ≈ 1.020150500625 * 1.005\n\n1.020150500625 * 1 = 1.020150500625\n\n1.020150500625 * 0.005 ≈ 0.0051007528125\n\nAdding: 1.020150500625 + 0.0051007528125 ≈ 1.0252512534375\n\n1.005^6 ≈ 1.0252512534375 * 1.005\n\n1.0252512534375 * 1 = 1.0252512534375\n\n1.0252512534375 * 0.005 ≈ 0.0051262567671875\n\nAdding: 1.0252512534375 + 0.0051262567671875 ≈ 1.0303775102046875\n\n1.005^7 ≈ 1.0303775102046875 * 1.005\n\n1.0303775102046875 * 1 = 1.0303775102046875\n\n1.0303775102046875 * 0.005 ≈ 0.0051518875505234375\n\nAdding: 1.0303775102046875 + 0.0051518875505234375 ≈ 1.0355293977552109375\n\n1.005^8 ≈ 1.0355293977552109375 * 1.005\n\n1.0355293977552109375 * 1 = 1.0355293977552109375\n\n1.0355293977552109375 * 0.005 ≈ 0.005177646987756464\n\nAdding: 1.0355293977552109375 + 0.005177646987756464 ≈ 1.040707044742967\n\n1.005^9 ≈ 1.040707044742967 * 1.005\n\n1.040707044742967 * 1 = 1.040707044742967\n\n1.040707044742967 * 0.005 ≈ 0.005203535224243435\n\nAdding: 1.040707044742967 + 0.005203535224243