he precise value is 6.17%.\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual rate is 6.17%.\n\nSo, to conclude, the answer is 6.17%, so \\boxed{6.17}\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.17}.\n\\boxed{6.17}\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return as a 6% annual interest rate compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe formula for the effective annual rate is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r_{\\text{nominal}}}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( r_{\\text{nominal}} \\) is the nominal annual interest rate (6% or 0.06).\n- \\( n \\) is the number of compounding periods per year (12 for monthly).\n\nSubstituting the values:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + 0.005\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = (1.005)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\nCalculating \\( (1.005)^{12} \\):\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.061678 \\]\n\nThus, the effective annual rate is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} \\approx 1.061678 - 1 = 0.061678 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ r \\approx 6.17\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.17}.",
