ternatively, using semi-continuous compounding, but that's not necessary here.\n\nWait, maybe I should use the formula for effective annual rate (EAR) which is \\( (1 + \\frac{r}{n})^n - 1 \\), so here, \\( \\frac{r}{n} = \\frac{0.06}{12} = 0.005 \\), so \\( (1.005)^{12} - 1 ≈ 1.061679 - 1 = 0.061679 \\), which is 6.1679%, so approximately 6.17%.\n\nYes, so 6.17%.\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is approximately 6.17%, so \\( r ≈ 6.17\\% \\).\n\nBut just to make sure, perhaps I can compute \\( (1.005)^{12} \\) step by step manually.\n\nCompute 1.005^1 = 1.005\n\n1.005^2 = 1.005 * 1.005 = 1.010025\n\n1.005^3 = 1.010025 * 1.005. Let me compute that:\n\n1.010025 * 1.005:\n\nMultiply 1.010025 by 1: 1.010025\n\nMultiply 1.010025 by 0.005: 0.005050125\n\nAdd them: 1.010025 + 0.005050125 = 1.015075125\n\nSo, 1.005^3 ≈ 1.015075\n\n1.005^4 = 1.015075 * 1.005\n\nCompute 1.015075 * 1.005:\n\n1.015075 * 1 = 1.015075\n\n1.015075 * 0.005 = 0.005075375\n\nAdd them: 1.015075 + 0.005075375 ≈ 1.020150375\n\nSo, 1.005^4 ≈ 1.020150\n\n1.005^5 = 1.020150 * 1.005\n\nCompute 1.020150 * 1.005:\n\n1.020150 * 1 = 1.020150\n\n1.020150 * 0.005 = 0.00510075\n\nAdd them: 1.020150 + 0.00510075 ≈ 1.02525075\n\nSo, 1.005^5 ≈ 1.025251\n\n1.005^6 = 1.025251 * 1.005\n\nCompute 1.025251 * 1.005:\n\n1.025251 * 1 = 1.025251\n\n1.025251 * 0.005 = 0.005126255\n\nAdd them: 1.025251 + 0.005126255 ≈ 1.030377255\n\nSo, 1.005^6 ≈ 1.030377\n\n1.005^7 = 1.030377 * 1.005\n\nCompute 1.030377 * 1.005:\n\n1.030377 * 1 = 1.030377\n\n1.030377 * 0.005 = 0.005151885\n\nAdd them: 1.030377 + 0.005151885 ≈ 1.035528885\n\nSo, 1.005^7 ≈ 1.035529\n\n1.005^8 = 1.035529 * 1.005\n\nCompute 1.035529 * 1.005:\n\n1.035529 * 1 = 1.035529\n\n1.035529 * 0.005 = 0.005177645\n\nAdd them: 1.035529 + 0.005177645 ≈ 1.040706645\n\nSo, 1.005^8 ≈ 1.040707\n\n1.005^9 = 1.040707 * 1.005\n\nCompute 1.040707 * 1.005:\n\n1.040707 * 1 = 1.040707\n\n1.040707 * 0.005 = 0.005203535\n\nAdd them: 1.040707 + 0.005203535 ≈ 1.045910535\n\n