ormula for effective annual rate:\n\nEAR = (1 + (r/n))^{n} - 1\n\nWhere r is the nominal interest rate, and n is the number of compounding periods per year.\n\nSo, substituting the values:\n\nEAR = (1 + 0.06/12)^12 - 1\n\nWhich is exactly what I did earlier.\n\nComputing 0.06 divided by 12 is 0.005.\n\nSo, 1 + 0.005 = 1.005.\n\n1.005 to the power of 12 is approximately 1.061678, as we saw earlier.\n\nSubtracting 1 gives 0.061678, which is 6.1678%.\n\nRounded to the nearest hundredth is 6.17%.\n\nSo, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the formula for EAR more directly.\n\nEAR = (1 + r/n)^n - 1.\n\nSo, that's where that formula comes from. So, in this case, n is 12, r is 0.06.\n\nSo, we can compute it as (1 + 0.06/12)^12 - 1.\n\nWhich is exactly what I did before.\n\nSo, all methods lead to the same result.\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is approximately 6.17%.\n\nSo, r is 6.17 when rounded to the nearest hundredth.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 6.17.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.17}.\n\\boxed{6.17}\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) percent for a bank account that compounds monthly at an annual interest rate of 6 percent, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe formula for the effective annual rate is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r_{\\text{nominal}}}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( r_{\\text{nominal}} = 6\\% = 0.06 \\)\n- \\( n = 12 \\) (since it compounds monthly)\n\nSubstituting the values into the formula:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\nFirst, compute the inside of the left side:\n\\[ 1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005 \\]\n\nNext, raise 1.005 to the power of 12:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.061678 \\]\n\nSubtract 1 from this result:\n\\[ 1.061678 - 1 = 0.061678 \\]\n\nConvert this to a percentage and round to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ 0.061678 \\approx 0.0617 \\]\n\\[ 0.0617 \\times 100 \\approx 6.17\\% \\]\n\nThus, the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6.17} \\]",
