onthly compounding equal to the amount after one year with annual compounding:\n\\[ P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = P \\left(1 + r \\right) \\]\n\nCanceling the principal \\( P \\) from both sides:\n\\[ \\left(1 + 0.005\\right)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nCalculating \\( (1.005)^{12} \\):\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.06066 \\]\n\nThus:\n\\[ 1 + r = 1.06066 \\]\n\\[ r = 1.06066 - 1 \\]\n\\[ r \\approx 0.06066 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ r \\approx 6.07\\% \\]\n\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.",
