 rate is approximately 6.17%.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.17} percent.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return as a bank account with an annual interest rate of 6% compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe compound interest formula for one year with monthly compounding is:\n\\[ A_{\\text{monthly}} = P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} \\]\n\nSince the amount after one year with monthly compounding should equal the amount after one year with annual compounding, we set:\n\\[ P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = P \\left(1 + r \\right) \\]\n\nThe principal \\( P \\) cancels out, leaving:\n\\[ \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nCalculating the inside of the left side:\n\\[ 1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005 \\]\n\nThus, the equation becomes:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nTo find \\( r \\), we need to compute \\( (1.005)^{12} \\):\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.061677809 \\]\n\nTherefore:\n\\[ r = 1.061677809 - 1 = 0.061677809 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ r \\approx 6.16778125938986\\% \\approx 6.17\\% \\]\n\nThus, the equivalent annual interest rate is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6.17} \\]",
