      "full_cot": "1.005^5 = 1.120150501 * 1.005 ≈ 1.025251002 } Hmm, perhaps I should just accept that after calculating, it's approximately 6.07%. So, r is 6.07%.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07\\%}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return as a 6% annual interest rate compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe compound interest formula for one year is:\n\\[ A = P \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n \\]\n\nGiven:\n- The nominal annual interest rate is 6%, which is 0.06 in decimal.\n- The interest is compounded monthly, so \\( n = 12 \\).\n\nWe set up the equation for the amount after one year with monthly compounding equal to the amount after one year with annual compounding:\n\\[ P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = P \\left(1 + r \\right) \\]\n\nThe principal \\( P \\) cancels out:\n\\[ \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nCalculate the inside of the left side:\n\\[ 1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005 \\]\n\nSo, the equation becomes:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nWe compute \\( (1.005)^{12} \\):\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.06066 \\]\n\nThus:\n\\[ 1 + r = 1.06066 \\]\n\\[ r = 1.06066 - 1 \\]\n\\[ r = 0.06066 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ r \\approx 0.0607 \\]\n\\[ r \\approx 6.07\\% \\]\n\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07\\%}.",
