15689, so 1 + r = 1.0615689, so r ≈ 0.0615689, which is approximately 6.15689%, which is about 6.16%. Wait, that conflicts with the previous step-by-step calculation which gave us approximately 6.066%. Hmm, that's a discrepancy. Which one is more accurate? I think the step-by-step multiplication is more accurate because it's just multiplying 1.005 twelve times, which is straightforward. The logarithm method might have introduced some error because of the approximation. So, I think 6.066% is more precise. Therefore, rounding to the nearest hundredth, it's 6.07%.\n\nWait, hold on, 6.066% is approximately 6.07% when rounded to the nearest hundredth. So, yeah, that's correct. So, the effective annual rate is approximately 6.07%. So, I think the answer is 6.07%.\n\nTherefore, after going through the calculations step by step, I conclude that the equivalent annual interest rate is 6.07%.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return if it were compounded annually, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR) for the given monthly compounding rate.\n\nGiven:\n- Annual nominal interest rate (\\( r_{\\text{monthly}} \\)) = 6% = 0.06\n- Compounded monthly, so \\( n = 12 \\)\n\nThe formula for the effective annual rate (EAR) is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r_{\\text{monthly}}}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + 0.005\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = (1.005)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\nCalculating \\( (1.005)^{12} \\):\nUsing step-by-step multiplication, we find:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.06066 \\]\n\nThus, the effective annual rate is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} \\approx 1.06066 - 1 = 0.06066 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ r \\approx 6.066\\% \\approx 6.07\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\(\\boxed{6.07}\\).",
