      "full_cot": "So, as we can see, it's approximately 1.60660127. 6.07}.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n\\\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) for a bank account that compounds monthly at an annual interest rate of 6 percent, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR). \n\nThe compound interest formula for monthly compounding is:\n\\[ A = P \\left(1 + \\frac{r_{\\text{monthly}}}{n}\\right)^n \\]\nwhere \\( r_{\\text{monthly}} = 0.06 \\) and \\( n = 12 \\).\n\nThe effective annual rate is given by:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r_{\\text{monthly}}}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\n\nSubstituting the values:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + 0.005\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = (1.005)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\nCalculating \\( (1.005)^{12} \\):\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.060660127 \\]\n\nThus:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = 1.060660127 - 1 \\approx 0.060660127 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ r \\approx 6.07\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.",
