      "full_cot": "So, subtracting 1 gives us 0.060660127, which is 0.0660127%. 6.07}\n\nWait, but wait a second, I think I made a mistake in my thought process. Let me double-check. So, the effective annual rate is approximately 6.066%, which should be rounded to 6.07%. So, r is 6.07%. Therefore, the answer is 6.07%.\n\nBut hold on, when I first started, I thought about using logarithms, but perhaps using the formula directly is more straightforward. Let me just confirm that the formula for EAR is correct. Yes, the effective annual rate is calculated as (1 + nominal rate / number of compounding periods)^number of compounding periods - 1. So, in this case, it's (1 + 0.06/12)^12 - 1, which is exactly what we calculated. So, 1.005^12 is approximately 1.06066, so subtracting 1 gives us 0.06066, which is 6.066%, so 6.07% when rounded to the nearest hundredth. Therefore, r is 6.07%.\n\nI think that's correct. I don't see any mistakes in the calculations now. So, I can confidently say that the equivalent annual interest rate is 6.07%.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return as a bank account with an annual interest rate of 6 percent compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe compound interest formula is:\n\\[ A = P \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n \\]\n\nFor monthly compounding, \\( n = 12 \\) and the nominal rate \\( r = 0.06 \\). We set the amount after one year equal for both monthly and annual compounding:\n\\[ P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = P \\left(1 + r \\right) \\]\n\nThe principal \\( P \\) cancels out, so we have:\n\\[ \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nCalculating the inside of the left side:\n\\[ 1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005 \\]\n\nThus, the equation becomes:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nWe compute \\( (1.005)^{12} \\) step by step:\n\\[ 1.005^1 = 1.005 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^2 = 1.010025 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^3 = 1.015075125 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^4 \\approx 1.020150501 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^5 \\approx 1.025251002 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^6 \\approx 1.030301502 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^7 \\approx 1.035355506 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^8 \\approx 1.040408016 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^9 \\approx 1.045461025 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^{10} \\approx 1.050525126 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^{11} \\approx 1.055600127 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^{12} \\approx 1.060660127 \\]\n\nThus, \\( (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.06066 \\). Therefore:\n\\[ 1 + r = 1.06066 \\]\n\\[ r = 1.06066 - 1 = 0.06066 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth, we get:\n\\[ r \\approx 6.07\\% \\]\n\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.",
