      "full_cot": "0.005 = 0.05 6.07}.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n\\\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return as a 6% annual interest rate compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\n1. The nominal annual interest rate is 6%, compounded monthly. The formula for compound interest is:\n   \\[\n   A = P \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n\n   \\]\n   where \\( r = 0.06 \\) and \\( n = 12 \\).\n\n2. To find the EAR, we set the amount after one year with monthly compounding equal to the amount after one year with annual compounding:\n   \\[\n   P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = P (1 + r)\n   \\]\n\n3. Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = 1 + r\n   \\]\n\n4. Compute \\( \\frac{0.06}{12} = 0.005 \\), so:\n   \\[\n   (1.005)^{12} = 1 + r\n   \\]\n\n5. Calculate \\( (1.005)^{12} \\):\n   \\[\n   (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.06066\n   \\]\n\n6. Therefore:\n   \\[\n   1 + r \\approx 1.06066 \\implies r \\approx 0.06066\n   \\]\n\n7. Converting to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n   \\[\n   r \\approx 6.07\\%\n   \\]\n\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.",
