      "full_cot": ") Compute Δx = 0.06 - 0.059849692 = 0.00150308 } 6.07\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) percent that would give the same return as a 6 percent annual interest rate compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe formula for the effective annual rate is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\n\nGiven:\n- Annual interest rate (\\( r \\)) = 6% = 0.06\n- Number of compounding periods per year (\\( n \\)) = 12\n\nFirst, compute the monthly interest rate:\n\\[ \\frac{0.06}{12} = 0.005 \\]\n\nNext, calculate the compound factor for monthly compounding:\n\\[ (1 + 0.005)^{12} \\]\n\nUsing the step-by-step multiplication:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.06066 \\]\n\nThis factor is then used to find the effective annual rate:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = 1.06066 - 1 = 0.06066 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ 0.06066 \\times 100 \\approx 6.066 \\approx 6.07 \\]\n\nThus, the equivalent annual interest rate is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6.07} \\]",
      "sentence_count": 17,
      "token_count": 307,
      "uncertainty_word_count": 0,
      "uncertainty_occurrences": [],
      "final_answer": "6.07",
      "flipped_chunk_idx": 109,
      "input_token_count": 2482,
      "is_correct": false,
      "flipped_chunk": ") Compute Δx = 0.06 - 0.059849692 = 0.00150308",
      "original_chunk": ") Compute Δx = 0.06 - 0.059849692 = 0.000150308"
