      "full_cot": "So, that's approximately 1.61677. } Well, wait, let me recap: (1.005)^12 ≈ 1.06066, so 1 + r = 1.06066, so r = 0.06066, which is 6.066%, so rounded to the nearest hundredth is 6.07%. Therefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is 6.07%.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n\\\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return as a 6% annual interest rate compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR). \n\nThe formula for the effective annual rate when interest is compounded monthly is:\n\\[\n\\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n - 1\n\\]\nwhere \\( r = 0.06 \\) and \\( n = 12 \\).\n\nFirst, compute the inside of the left side:\n\\[\n1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005\n\\]\n\nNext, raise this to the 12th power:\n\\[\n(1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.06066\n\\]\n\nSubtract 1 to find the effective annual rate:\n\\[\n\\text{EAR} = 1.06066 - 1 = 0.06066\n\\]\n\nConvert this to a percentage and round to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[\nr = 0.06066 \\approx 6.07\\%\n\\]\n\nThus, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.",
