      "full_cot": "So, that's approximately 6.107%. } Wait, but earlier step-by-step multiplication gave us 1.06066, which is approximately 6.066%, but the logarithm method gave us about 6.168%. There is a discrepancy here. Wait, maybe I made a mistake in one of the calculations.\n\nWait, let me check: when I computed step by step, 1.005^12 ≈ 1.060660127. But with logarithms, I got about 1.06168. There is a difference. Hmm, so perhaps the step-by-step multiplication was more accurate, as it was 12 multiplications, each precise.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps my logarithm approach had some approximation errors.\n\nWait, let's try to calculate 1.005^12 using a different method.\n\nCompute 1.005^12:\n\nFirst, compute 1.005 squared: (1.005)^2 = 1.010025\n\nThen, (1.010025)^2 = 1.020150501\n\n(1.020150501)^2 ≈ 1.040408016\n\n(1.040408016)^2 ≈ 1.082432102\n\nWait, wait, that can't be. Because 1.040408016 squared is 1.082432102? Wait, 1.04 squared is 1.0816, so 1.040408016 squared is approximately 1.0824, yes. But wait, 1.005^12 is actually 1.005 multiplied 12 times, so the process is as follows:\n\nWait, perhaps the way I squared it was wrong.\n\nWait, maybe a better approach is to use the exponentiation step by step:\n\n1.005^1 = 1.005\n\n1.005^2 = 1.005 * 1.005 = 1.010025\n\n1.005^3 = 1.010025 * 1.005 ≈ 1.015075125\n\n1.005^4 ≈ 1.015075125 * 1.005 ≈ 1.020150501\n\n1.005^5 ≈ 1.020150501 * 1.005 ≈ 1.025251002\n\n1.005^6 ≈ 1.025251002 * 1.005 ≈ 1.030301502\n\n1.005^7 ≈ 1.030301502 * 1.005 ≈ 1.035355506\n\n1.005^8 ≈ 1.035355506 * 1.005 ≈ 1.040408016\n\n1.005^9 ≈ 1.040408016 * 1.005 ≈ 1.045461025\n\n1.005^10 ≈ 1.045461025 * 1.005 ≈ 1.050525126\n\n1.005^11 ≈ 1.050525126 * 1.005 ≈ 1.055600127\n\n1.005^12 ≈ 1.055600127 * 1.005 ≈ 1.060660127\n\nSo, step-by-step, it's 1.060660127. So, that is about 1.06066. So, that is about 6.066%.\n\nBut when I used the logarithm method, I got approximately 1.06168, which is about 6.168%. There is a discrepancy here. Hmm. So, which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe my logarithm method was incorrect because I made an error in the approximation.\n\nWait, let me compute 12 * ln(1.005) more accurately.\n\nCompute ln(1.005): Using more precise computation.\n\nWe can use the Taylor series expansion around 0: ln(1+x) = x - x^2/2 + x^3/3 - x^4/4 + x^5/5 - ...\n\nBut for x = 0.005, the terms get smaller quickly, but let's compute it more accurately.\n\nCompute ln(1.005):\n\nx = 0.005\n\nln(1.005) = 0.005 - (0.005)^2 / 2 + (0.005)^3 / 3 - (0.005)^4 / 4 + (0.005)^5 / 5 - ...\n\nCompute each term:\n\n0.005 = 0.005\n\n(0.005)^2 = 0.000025; 0.000025 / 2 = 0.0000125\n\n(0.005)^3 = 0.000000125; 0.000000125 / 3 ≈ 0.0000000416667\n\n(0.005)^4 = 0.000000000625; 0.000000000625 / 4 ≈ 0.00000000015625\n\n(0.005)^5 = 0.000000000003125; 0.000000000003125 / 5 ≈ 0.000000000000625\n\nSo, adding up:\n\n0.005 - 0.0000125 = 0.0049875\n\n0.0049875 + 0.0000000416667 ≈ 0.0049875416667\n\n0.0049875416667 - 0.00000000015625 ≈ 0.0049875415104\n\n0.0049875415104 + 0.000000000000625 ≈ 0.0049875415104\n\nSo, ln(1.005) ≈ 0.00498754151\n\nMultiply by 12: 12 * 0.00498754151 ≈ 0.05984969212\n\nSo, ln(1.005^12) = 12 * ln(1.005) ≈ 0.05984969212\n\nTherefore, 1.005^12 = e^{0.05984969212}\n\nCompute e^{0.05984969212}:\n\nWe can use the Taylor series expansion around x=0 for e^x, which is 1 + x + x^2 / 2! + x^3 / 3! + x^4 / 4! + ...\n\nLet me compute up to the x^4 term for better accuracy.\n\nx = 0.05984969212\n\nCompute e^x:\n\n1 + x + x^2 / 2 + x^3 / 6 + x^4 / 24\n\nCompute each term:\n\n1 = 1\n\nx = 0.05984969212\n\nx^2 = (0.05984969212)^2 ≈ 0.003582\n\nx^2 / 2 ≈ 0.001791\n\nx^3 ≈ (0.05984969212)^3 ≈ 0.000215\n\nx^3 / 6 ≈ 0.0000358\n\nx^4 ≈ (0.05984969212)^4 ≈ 0.0000128\n\nx^4 / 24 ≈ 0.000000533\n\nSo, adding up:\n\n1 + 0.05984969212 = 1.05984969212\n\n1.05984969212 + 0.001791 ≈ 1.06164069212\n\n1.06164069212 + 0.0000358 ≈ 1.06167649212\n\n1.06167649212 + 0.000000533 ≈ 1.06167702512\n\nSo, e^{0.05984969212} ≈ 1.06167702512\n\nTherefore, 1.005^12 ≈ 1.06167702512\n\nSo, that gives us 1.06167702512, which is approximately 1.06168, so \\( 1 + r = 1.06168 \\), so \\( r = 0.06168 \\), which is 6.168%. So, now, this conflicts with my earlier step-by-step multiplication which gave me 1.06066.\n\nWait, so which one is correct? Hmm.\n\nWait, let me verify with an online calculator. Since I can't access an external resource, I'll try to compute 1.005^12 more accurately.\n\nCompute 1.005^12:\n\n1.005^1 = 1.005\n\n1.005^2 = 1.005 * 1.005 = 1.010025\n\n1.005^3 = 1.010025 * 1.005: 1.010025 * 1 = 1.010025; 1.010025 * 0.005 = 0.005050125; total = 1.015075125\n\n1.005^4 = 1.015075125 * 1.005: 1.015075125 * 1 = 1.015075125; 1.015075125 * 0.005 = 0.005075375625; total ≈ 1.020150500625\n\n1.005^5 = 1.020150500625 * 1.005: 1.020150500625 * 1 = 1.020150500625; 1.020150500625 * 0.005 = 0.0051007528125; total ≈ 1.0252512534375\n\n1.005^6 = 1.0252512534375 * 1.005: 1.0252512534375 * 1 = 1.0252512534375; 1.0252512534375 * 0.005 = 0.0051262567671875; total ≈ 1.0303775102047\n\nWait, wait, I think I messed up here. Let me redo 1.005^6.\n\nWait, 1.005^5 ≈ 1.0252512534375\n\n1.005^6 = 1.0252512534375 * 1.005: Multiply 1.0252512534375 by 1.005.\n\n1.0252512534375 * 1 = 1.0252512534375\n\n1.0252512534375 * 0.005 = 0.0051262567671875\n\nSo, adding together: 1.0252512534375 + 0.0051262567671875 = 1.0303775102047\n\nSo, 1.005^6 ≈ 1.0303775102047\n\n1.005^7 = 1.0303775102047 * 1.005: 1.0303775102047 * 1 = 1.0303775102047; 1.0303775102047 * 0.005 = 0.00515188755023185; total ≈ 1.0355293977549\n\n1.005^8 = 1.0355293977549 * 1.005: 1.0355293977549 * 1 = 1.0355293977549; 1.0355293977549 * 0.005 ≈ 0.00517764698874745; total ≈ 1.0407070447436\n\n1.005^9 = 1.0407070447436 * 1.005: 1.0407070447436 * 1 = 1.0407070447436; 1.0407070447436 * 0.005 ≈ 0.005203535223182; total ≈ 1.0459105799668\n\n1.005^10 = 1.0459105799668 * 1.005: 1.0459105799668 * 1 = 1.0459105799668; 1.0459105799668 * 0.005 ≈ 0.005229552899834; total ≈ 1.0511401328666\n\n1.005^11 = 1.0511401328666 