uivalent to a bank account that compounds annually at a rate of r percent, then what is r?\" So, since the monthly compounding at 6% is equivalent to an annual compounding rate of approximately 6.17%.\n\nTherefore, r is approximately 6.17%.\n\nBut wait, I have to be careful here because in some textbooks, the EAR is calculated as (1 + r/n)^n -1, and that's exactly what we did here, so 1.0616778 -1 = 0.0616778, so 6.16778%, which rounds to 6.17%.\n\nSo, conclusion: r ≈ 6.17%\n\nBut",
