9396319375 * 1.005 = 1.035529396319375 + 1.035529396319375 * 0.005 ≈ 1.035529396319375 + 0.00517764698196875 ≈ 1.0407070433013448\n\n1.005^8 ≈ 1.0407070433013448.\n\n1.0407070433013448 * 1.005 = 1.0407070433013448 + 1.0407070433013448 * 0.005 ≈ 1.0407070433013448 + 0.00520353521568224 ≈ 1.045910578516027\n\n1.005^9 ≈ 1.045910578516027.\n\n1.045910578516027 * 1.005 = 1.045910578516027 + 1.045910578516027 * 0.005 ≈ 1.045910578516027 + 0.005229552893080135 ≈ 1.051140131409107\n\n1.005^10 ≈ 1.051140131409107.\n\n1.051140131409107 * 1.005 = 1.051140131409107 + 1.051140131409107 * 0.005 ≈ 1.051140131409107 + 0.00525570065654535 ≈ 1.056395832065652\n\n1.005^11 ≈ 1.056395832065652.\n\n1.056395832065652 * 1.005 = 1.056395832065652 + 1.056395832065652 * 0.005 ≈ 1.056395832065652 + 0.00528197916132826 ≈ 1.061677811226980\n\n1.005^12 ≈ 1.061677811226980.\n\nSo, that's the exact calculation. Therefore, \\( (1.005)^{12} ≈ 1.0616778112 \\). Therefore, subtracting 1, we get r ≈ 0.0616778112, which is 6.16778112%. So, 6.16778112% is approximately 6.17% when rounded to the nearest hundredth.\n\nSo, earlier, my step-by-step was wrong because I stopped at 1.06066, which was incorrect. So, the correct value is approximately 6.17%. Therefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is 6.17%.\n\nWait, but in my first calculation, I thought that 1.005^12 was 1.06066, but actually, it's approximately 1.06168, so 6.17%.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 6.17%.\n\nBut hold on, earlier I thought about 6.066%, but that was incorrect because I didn't carry out the multiplication correctly. So, the correct answer is 6.17%.\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.17}.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.17}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) for a bank account that compounds monthly at an annual interest rate of 6 percent, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe formula for the effective annual rate is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\nwhere \\( r \\) is the nominal annual interest rate and \\( n \\) is the number of compounding periods per year.\n\nGiven:\n- The nominal annual interest rate \\( r = 6\\% = 0.06 \\)\n- The compounding period \\( n = 12 \\) (monthly)\n\nSubstituting the values into the formula:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + 0.005\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = (1.005)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\nCalculating \\( (1.005)^{12} \\):\nUsing the step-by-step multiplication method, we find:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.0616778 \\]\n\nThus, the effective annual rate is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = 1.0616778 - 1 \\approx 0.0616778 \\]\nConverting this to a percentage:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} \\approx 6.1678\\% \\]\n\nRounding to the nearest hundredth, we get:\n\\[ r \\approx 6.17\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.17}.",
