e same return if compounded annually instead of monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR) for the given monthly compounding rate.\n\nGiven:\n- Annual nominal interest rate, \\( r_{\\text{monthly}} = 6\\% = 0.06 \\)\n- Compounded monthly, so \\( n = 12 \\)\n\nThe formula for the effective annual rate (EAR) is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r_{\\text{monthly}}}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + 0.005\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = (1.005)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\nWe need to compute \\( (1.005)^{12} \\). Using step-by-step multiplication:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n1.005^1 & = 1.005 \\\\\n1.005^2 & = 1.010025 \\\\\n1.005^3 & = 1.015075125 \\\\\n1.005^4 & = 1.020150501 \\\\\n1.005^5 & = 1.025251002 \\\\\n1.005^6 & = 1.030301502 \\\\\n1.005^7 & = 1.035355506 \\\\\n1.005^8 & = 1.040408016 \\\\\n1.005^9 & = 1.045461025 \\\\\n1.005^{10} & = 1.050525126 \\\\\n1.005^{11} & = 1.055600127 \\\\\n1.005^{12} & = 1.060660127 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThus, \\( (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.060660127 \\). Therefore:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = 1.060660127 - 1 = 0.060660127 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ 0.060660127 \\approx 0.0607 \\]\n\\[ r \\approx 6.07\\% \\]\n\nHence, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\(\\boxed{6.07}\\).",
