      "full_cot": "1.005^2 = 1.005 6.07}.\n\nWait, sorry, hold on. The step-by-step computation gave us approximately 1.06066, which is 6.066%, so 6.07% when rounded to the nearest hundredth. The logarithm method gave me approximately 1.06168, which is 6.168%, so 6.17%. Which one is correct? Hmm, I think the step-by-step multiplication is more accurate because each step is precise, so 1.005^12 is approximately 1.0606601, so 6.066%, which is 6.07%. So, I think 6.07% is correct.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the formula for the effective annual rate directly. The formula is: \\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\] Where r is the nominal annual rate, and n is the number of compounding periods per year. So, plugging in r = 6% and n = 12: \\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} - 1 \\] Which is exactly what I did earlier. So, 1.005^12 is approximately 1.06066, so EAR is approximately 6.066%, which rounds to 6.07%. Therefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is 6.07%.\n\nJust to confirm, I think the exact value of 1.005^12 is approximately 1.0606601, so 6.066%, which is 6.07% when rounded to the nearest hundredth. So, I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) percent that would give the same return as an account compounded monthly at a rate of 6 percent, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR). The formula for the effective annual rate is:\n\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\n\nwhere \\( r \\) is the nominal annual interest rate and \\( n \\) is the number of compounding periods per year. Here, \\( r = 0.06 \\) and \\( n = 12 \\).\n\nFirst, we compute the inside of the left side of the formula:\n\n\\[ 1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005 \\]\n\nNext, we raise this to the 12th power:\n\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.0606601 \\]\n\nThis value is then subtracted by 1 to find the EAR:\n\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = 1.0606601 - 1 = 0.0606601 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth, we get:\n\n\\[ 0.0606601 \\approx 0.0607 \\]\n\nThus, the equivalent annual interest rate is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{6.07} \\]",
