      "full_cot": "1.005^3 = 1.012025 * 1.005 = 1.015075125 6.07\\%}\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07\\%}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return as a bank account with an annual interest rate of 6 percent compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe compound interest formula is:\n\\[ A = P \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n \\]\n\nFor the given problem, we consider the amount after one year with both monthly and annual compounding. Setting these amounts equal, we get:\n\\[ P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = P \\left(1 + r \\right) \\]\n\nThe principal \\( P \\) cancels out, leaving:\n\\[ \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nCalculating the inside of the left side:\n\\[ 1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005 \\]\n\nThus, the equation becomes:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nWe need to compute \\( (1.005)^{12} \\). Using step-by-step multiplication:\n\\[ 1.005^1 = 1.005 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^2 = 1.010025 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^3 = 1.015075125 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^4 = 1.020150501 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^5 = 1.025251002 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^6 = 1.030301502 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^7 = 1.035355506 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^8 = 1.040408016 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^9 = 1.045461025 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^{10} = 1.050525126 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^{11} = 1.055600127 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^{12} = 1.060660127 \\]\n\nThus, \\( (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.060660127 \\). Therefore:\n\\[ 1 + r = 1.060660127 \\]\n\\[ r = 1.060660127 - 1 = 0.060660127 \\]\n\nRounding to the nearest hundredth, we get:\n\\[ r \\approx 0.0607 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage, the equivalent annual interest rate is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6.07\\%} \\]",
