      "full_cot": "1.005^4 = 1.015075125 * 1.005 ≈ 1.20150501 } 6.07\n\nWait, no, actually, hold on. Let me just compute 1.005^12 using more accurate multiplication. Let me use a calculator approach:\n\n1.005^1 = 1.005\n\n1.005^2 = 1.005 * 1.005 = 1.010025\n\n1.005^3 = 1.010025 * 1.005 = 1.015075125\n\n1.005^4 = 1.015075125 * 1.005 = 1.020150501\n\n1.005^5 = 1.020150501 * 1.005 = 1.025251002\n\n1.005^6 = 1.025251002 * 1.005 = 1.030301502\n\n1.005^7 = 1.030301502 * 1.005 = 1.035355506\n\n1.005^8 = 1.035355506 * 1.005 = 1.040408016\n\n1.005^9 = 1.040408016 * 1.005 = 1.045461025\n\n1.005^10 = 1.045461025 * 1.005 = 1.050525126\n\n1.005^11 = 1.050525126 * 1.005 = 1.055600127\n\n1.005^12 = 1.055600127 * 1.005 = 1.060660127\n\nSo, 1.005^12 is approximately 1.060660127. Therefore, subtracting 1, the effective annual rate is approximately 0.060660127, or 6.0660127%. Rounded to the nearest hundredth, that's 6.07%. Therefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is 6.07%.\n\nAlternatively, to cross-verify, let me compute the amount after one year for both monthly and annual compounding and see if they are equal when r is 6.07%.\n\nAssume P = $1 for simplicity.\n\nWith monthly compounding:\nAmount = 1 * (1 + 0.06/12)^12 = 1 * (1.005)^12 ≈ 1.060660127\n\nWith annual compounding:\nAmount = 1 * (1 + 0.0607) = 1.0607\n\nSo, 1.0607 vs 1.060660127. They are very close, with a difference due to rounding. So, this further confirms that 6.07% is the correct rounded value.\n\nTherefore, after carefully computing, I can conclude that the equivalent annual interest rate is 6.07%.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return as a 6% annual interest rate compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe formula for the effective annual rate is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\nwhere \\( r \\) is the annual interest rate (6% or 0.06) and \\( n \\) is the number of compounding periods per year (12 for monthly).\n\nFirst, compute the inside of the left side:\n\\[ 1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005 \\]\n\nNext, raise this value to the power of 12:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.060660127 \\]\n\nThis result gives us the factor by which the principal grows in one year. Subtracting 1 from this factor gives the effective annual rate:\n\\[ 1.060660127 - 1 = 0.060660127 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ 0.060660127 \\approx 0.0607 \\]\nThus, \\( r \\) is 6.07%.\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6.07} \\]",
