      "full_cot": "1.005^6 ≈ 1.025251002 * 1.005 ≈ 0.030301502 06.07} Wait, no, in the problem, the answer needs to be in a box, and probably as \\boxed{6.07}. But let me just verify once again.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the formula for EAR:\n\nEAR = (1 + (r/n))^n - 1\n\nSo, r = 6% per annum, n = 12.\n\nEAR = (1 + 6/12)^12 - 1 = (1.005)^12 - 1.\n\nAs we calculated earlier, (1.005)^12 ≈ 1.0606601.\n\nSo, EAR ≈ 1.0606601 - 1 = 0.0606601, which is 6.06601%.\n\nRounded to the nearest hundredth is 6.07%.\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is 6.07%.\n\nSo, the answer is 6.07%, which in a box is \\boxed{6.07}.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n</think>\n\nDr. Fu Manchu has a bank account with an annual interest rate of 6 percent, compounded monthly. We need to find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return if compounded annually.\n\nFirst, we use the formula for compound interest. The compound interest formula is:\n\\[ A = P \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n \\]\nwhere \\( A \\) is the amount of money accumulated after \\( n \\) years, including interest, \\( P \\) is the principal amount, \\( r \\) is the annual interest rate (decimal), and \\( n \\) is the number of times that interest is compounded per year.\n\nSince we are looking for the equivalent annual rate after one year, we set the amount after one year with monthly compounding equal to the amount after one year with annual compounding:\n\\[ P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = P \\left(1 + r \\right) \\]\n\nThe principal \\( P \\) cancels out, leaving:\n\\[ \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nWe compute the inside of the left side:\n\\[ 1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005 \\]\n\nSo, the equation becomes:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nWe need to calculate \\( (1.005)^{12} \\). Using step-by-step multiplication:\n\\[ 1.005^1 = 1.005 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^2 = 1.010025 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^3 = 1.015075125 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^4 \\approx 1.020150501 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^5 \\approx 1.025251002 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^6 \\approx 1.030301502 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^7 \\approx 1.035355506 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^8 \\approx 1.040408016 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^9 \\approx 1.045461025 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^{10} \\approx 1.050525126 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^{11} \\approx 1.055600127 \\]\n\\[ 1.005^{12} \\approx 1.060660127 \\]\n\nThus, \\( (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.06066 \\). Therefore:\n\\[ 1 + r \\approx 1.06066 \\]\n\\[ r \\approx 0.06066 \\]\n\nRounded to the nearest hundredth, \\( r \\) is 6.07%.\n\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.",
