\\text{monthly}} = P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} \\]\n\nFor the annual compounding:\n\\[ A_{\\text{annual}} = P \\left(1 + r \\right) \\]\n\nSetting these equal for one year:\n\\[ \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nSimplifying:\n\\[ \\left(1 + 0.005\\right)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nCalculating \\( (1.005)^{12} \\) step-by-step:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.060660127 \\]\n\nThus:\n\\[ 1 + r \\approx 1.060660127 \\]\n\\[ r \\approx 0.060660127 \\]\n\nConverting to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ r \\approx 6.07\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6.07}\n\\]",
