      "full_cot": "1.005^12 ≈ 1.055600127 * 1.005 ≈ 10.060660127 6.07}.\n\nWait, but the calculation is giving me 1.060660127, which is approximately 1.06066, so subtracting 1 gives 0.06066, which is approximately 6.066%, which rounds to 6.07%. So, that's consistent with the earlier result.\n\nWait, but in the logarithm method, I got 1.06168, which is 6.168%, which would round to 6.17%, but that seems inconsistent. Maybe my logarithm approach was off because of the approximation.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can use the formula for EAR again. The formula is:\n\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\n\nSo, plugging in r = 6% and n = 12:\n\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + 0.005\\right)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = (1.005)^{12} - 1 \\]\n\nWhich is exactly what we have. So, as per the calculation, (1.005)^12 ≈ 1.060660127, so EAR ≈ 0.060660127, which is 6.0660127%. Rounded to the nearest hundredth is 6.07%.\n\nSo, I think the correct answer is 6.07%.\n\nBut just to make sure, let me check with a calculator. Let me compute 1.005^12 on a calculator.\n\n1.005^1 = 1.005\n\n1.005^2 = 1.005 * 1.005 = 1.010025\n\n1.005^3 = 1.010025 * 1.005 ≈ 1.015075125\n\n1.005^4 = 1.015075125 * 1.005 ≈ 1.020150501\n\n1.005^5 ≈ 1.020150501 * 1.005 ≈ 1.025251002\n\n1.005^6 ≈ 1.025251002 * 1.005 ≈ 1.030301502\n\n1.005^7 ≈ 1.030301502 * 1.005 ≈ 1.035355506\n\n1.005^8 ≈ 1.035355506 * 1.005 ≈ 1.040408016\n\n1.005^9 ≈ 1.040408016 * 1.005 ≈ 1.045461025\n\n1.005^10 ≈ 1.045461025 * 1.005 ≈ 1.050525126\n\n1.005^11 ≈ 1.050525126 * 1.005 ≈ 1.055600127\n\n1.005^12 ≈ 1.055600127 * 1.005 ≈ 1.060660127\n\nSo, 1.005^12 = 1.060660127. So, EAR = 1.060660127 - 1 = 0.060660127, which is 6.0660127%, which is approximately 6.07% when rounded to the nearest hundredth.\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is 6.07%.\n\nWait, but just to make sure, let me use another approach. Let me use the formula for compound interest for one year and set it equal to the amount after one year with annual compounding. Let me denote:\n\nAmount after one year with monthly compounding: \\( A = P(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12})^{12} \\)\n\nAmount after one year with annual compounding: \\( A = P(1 + r) \\)\n\nSince both amounts are equal, set them equal:\n\n\\( P(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12})^{12} = P(1 + r) \\)\n\nCancel P from both sides:\n\n\\( (1 + \\frac{0.06}{12})^{12} = 1 + r \\)\n\nCompute \\( \\frac{0.06}{12} = 0.005 \\)\n\nSo,\n\n\\( (1.005)^{12} = 1 + r \\)\n\nCompute \\( (1.005)^{12} \\) as 1.060660127\n\nSo, \\( 1 + r = 1.060660127 \\)\n\nTherefore, \\( r = 1.060660127 - 1 = 0.060660127 \\), which is 6.0660127%. Rounded to the nearest hundredth is 6.07%.\n\nSo, yes, this confirms the earlier result.\n\nAlternatively, if I use a financial calculator, it would compute (1.005)^12 as approximately 1.0606601, leading to the same conclusion.\n\nSo, the equivalent annual interest rate is 6.07%.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 6.07.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return as a bank account that compounds monthly at an annual interest rate of 6 percent, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe formula for the effective annual rate is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\n\nGiven:\n- The annual interest rate \\( r = 6\\% = 0.06 \\)\n- The compounding frequency \\( n = 12 \\) (since it compounds monthly)\n\nFirst, compute the monthly interest rate:\n\\[ \\frac{0.06}{12} = 0.005 \\]\n\nNext, calculate the compound factor for one year:\n\\[ (1 + 0.005)^{12} \\]\n\nUsing step-by-step multiplication:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.060660127 \\]\n\nThus, the effective annual rate is:\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = 1.060660127 - 1 = 0.060660127 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ 0.060660127 \\approx 0.0607 \\]\n\\[ \\text{EAR} \\approx 6.07\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the equivalent annual interest rate is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6.07} \\]",
