    {
      "full_cot": "**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n\n================================================================================\nEND OF CHUNKS\n================================================================================ 6.07}.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) for a bank account that compounds monthly at an annual rate of 6 percent, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR). The formula for the effective annual rate is:\n\n\\[ \\text{EAR} = \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n - 1 \\]\n\nwhere \\( r \\) is the annual interest rate (6%) and \\( n \\) is the number of compounding periods per year (12 for monthly compounding).\n\n1. Calculate the monthly interest rate:\n   \\[ \\frac{0.06}{12} = 0.005 \\]\n\n2. Compute the factor by which the principal grows in one year with monthly compounding:\n   \\[ (1 + 0.005)^{12} \\]\n\n3. Using the step-by-step multiplication method:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   1.005^1 & = 1.005 \\\\\n   1.005^2 & = 1.010025 \\\\\n   1.005^3 & = 1.015075125 \\\\\n   1.005^4 & \\approx 1.020150501 \\\\\n   1.005^5 & \\approx 1.025251002 \\\\\n   1.005^6 & \\approx 1.030301502 \\\\\n   1.005^7 & \\approx 1.035355506 \\\\\n   1.005^8 & \\approx 1.040408016 \\\\\n   1.005^9 & \\approx 1.045461025 \\\\\n   1.005^{10} & \\approx 1.050525126 \\\\\n   1.005^{11} & \\approx 1.055600127 \\\\\n   1.005^{12} & \\approx 1.060660127 \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n4. Subtract 1 from the result to find the EAR:\n   \\[ 1.060660127 - 1 = 0.060660127 \\]\n\n5. Convert this to a percentage and round to the nearest hundredth:\n   \\[ 0.060660127 \\approx 0.0607 \\]\n\nThus, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\(\\boxed{6.07}\\).",
